# C1-S02 — Stew. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1572–1624.
# Elara's house. The game slows down: the player can ask the basic questions
# here instead of having them dumped on the road. Each topic can be asked
# once. Inspectable objects have their own nodes.

~ start
do elara_serves_stew
Kaelen: This smells amazing. What is it?
Elara: Stew.
Kaelen: That's a category, not a recipe.
Elara: Today it's both. Eat. You've the face of someone who forgot meals existed somewhere around noon.
=> topics

~ topics
? Kaelen (Internal): Ask her something?
- [if not ch1_stew_asked_where] So where am I, exactly? Properly, this time. => where
- [if not ch1_stew_asked_fracture] What's the Fracture? The short version. => fracture
- [if not ch1_stew_asked_magic] How does magic work here? Is there a rule to it? => magic
- [if not ch1_elara_arm_talked] About your arm... can I ask? => arm
- (Just eat.) => END

~ where
set ch1_stew_asked_where
Elara: Aethelgard. You asked me that on the road.
Kaelen: I know. It didn't stick. Is it a country? I'd like something today to be just a country.
Elara: It's the world. All of it.
Kaelen: Of course it is. Why would it be any— no. Then they're in it. All of them, somewhere in it.
Elara: It's big enough to hold them. Finish the bowl before you go looking.
=> topics

~ fracture
set ch1_stew_asked_fracture
Elara: It's when things stop agreeing with themselves. Trees, water, roads. People, sometimes.
Kaelen: Things not agreeing with themselves. And that's the official version?
Elara: It's the useful one. The priests have a longer one with more stars in it. It's never moved a cart.
=> topics

~ magic
set ch1_stew_asked_magic
Elara: You're asking me? You're the one who reached inside a beast this afternoon.
Kaelen: That wasn't me reaching, it was— I don't know what it was. Can I finish the stew before I find out?
=> topics

~ arm
set ch1_elara_arm_talked
[if elara_arm_respected_silence] => arm_waited
=> arm_pushed

~ arm_waited
Elara: You waited. On the road, when I did the cart. You saw, and you didn't say anything.
Kaelen: You didn't look like you wanted it talked about. I've worn that look myself.
Elara: I still don't.
Kaelen: Then we won't. Is there more of this, or did I eat yours?
Elara: ...Thank you, stranger.
do trust elara 10
=> topics

~ arm_pushed
Elara: It's corruption. It's been there years. Every time I cast, it gets a little worse.
Kaelen: Then stop casting.
do pause 1.2
Elara: There it is.
Kaelen: There what is?
Elara: Stranger turns up, sees one afternoon of my life, and solves it.
Kaelen: I didn't mean it like that. I just— something's wrong, and I go straight for the fix.
Elara: I know you didn't. That's why I'm only annoyed with you.
=> topics

# ── Things in the room ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

~ inspect_bandages
Kaelen (Internal): Bandages. A lot of them, rolled and ready. More than one person ought to need.
do elara_sees_him_look
Elara: They're mine, before you ask.
Kaelen: I wasn't going to ask.
Elara: You were. Your face asks before your mouth does.

~ inspect_herbs
Kaelen (Internal): Half of these I don't recognise. The rest I'd only know in a jar, with a label on it.

~ inspect_focuses
Kaelen (Internal): Three cracked... wands? Foci? Whatever they are, she goes through them fast. Faster than she should.

~ inspect_cloak
Kaelen (Internal): Patched so many times there's more patch than cloak. Every stitch is neat, though.

~ inspect_map
Kaelen (Internal): Oakhaven, the crater, a road going south. Someone's drawn a skull over the north field.

# After the road ledger, on the way to her house.
~ invite
Elara: You're swaying, stranger. Food first, then you can worry about roads.
